 "notes": "Kirby Avenue: printed KIRBY AVE. in the north and KIRBY near Chase; taken as continuous down the SE diagonal past Schneider. The avenue leaving Kirby SW at the fork (2690,1522), crossing Tarrant and reaching Bruce at about (2083,3225), has only AVE. printed in this strip: '?'. Street west of Kirby at y 1313 printed only ST.: '?'. N-S street x 3520 (Otte to Frederick, printed ST.) continues by a jog to Schneider, Glen Parker and Bruce, where INNES is printed (suffix not legible; 'Innes Avenue' used throughout). Unnamed AVE. from Bruce (3728,3413) south past Westmoreland, Howland Place, Pullan, Ella to Chase (3733,5152): '?'; Pitts Street leaves Chase southward 26 px west of it (3707,5152). Bruce at Kirby: west arm meets Kirby centre at about (3055,3445), east arm at (3053,3418); one cross recorded. Bruce east of Kirby has no name printed in the strip (assumed Bruce). Street along the bottom plate edge (Kirby, Gordon, Pitts, Witler, Florida crossings) printed only ST.: '?'; its centre taken midway between block line and plate cut. Glen Armand: name runs off strip, suffix assumed. Hamilton/Otte and Glen Armand lie at x 4352, just past the 300 px margin; Bruce west end at x 2083 likewise. Strip x 3855-3900 between Otte and y 900 (printed 30) and strip x 3216-3246 south of Glen Parker (lot 126) read as lots, not streets. Hemlock Alley and an alley printed ALLEY meet Florida from the west. Solid lines inside streets are water pipes; street edges taken at block lines. | Names not legible on the plate are '?'. (1) The 50 ft north-south street from Otte Street through Philomena to Frederick Avenue (x about 3521-3526) is printed '... ST.' with the name overprinted by pipe labels; it is the same line as Innes (label INNES near y 3100, suffix not read; written Innes Avenue) which continues by a jog to Schneider, Glen Parker and the east-west street at y 3424. (2) The east-west street at y about 3424 from Kirby Avenue east past Innes (addresses 1640-1713; 21 in. sewer) has no name printed inside the strip. (3) The north-south avenue from that street south past Westmoreland, Howland Place, Pullan, Ella to Chase (x 3700-3824) is printed 'AVE.' with an illegible name. (4) The street entering Kirby Avenue from the west at y 1324 is printed only 'ST.' in the strip. (5) The avenue running south-west from the Kirby / Schneider junction (only 'AVE.' printed here) is taken as Virginia Avenue from the VIRGINIA label south of Chase; the avenue from Bruce south to Chase (only 'AVE.' legible) is taken as Florida Avenue, which it joins in line across Chase. Kirby / Schneider / Virginia is one five-armed junction (two entries a few px apart); Kirby / Bruce and Kirby / the y-3424 street are opposite arms 27 px apart; Chase / Pitts and Chase / the unnamed avenue are opposite arms about 30 px apart. Glen Parker Avenue meets Hamilton twice: the west part at (4065,1877) and the part continuing north-east at (4170,1946). Pell / Gordon and Gordon / Howland are L corners. Suffixes of Pitts, Ella, Florida, Innes not read (assumed). JESTER is as printed. Hanfield Street's south side is the plate edge; its centre is taken midway between the north building line and the plate edge. Henry Sr. & Aug. Freudenberg near (2250,2700) is an owner name, not a street. Otte / Hamilton (about 4366,290) and Haight / Hamilton lie east of x 4300 and are not picked."
